# Core rules

1. These are prototypes of **Power BI reports**, not GOV.UK services. The final build is Power BI. Only design what Power BI can do with native visuals and features (see `project/power-bi-feasibility.mdc`). If something can't be built in Power BI, say so. Don't improvise a workaround silently.
2. Accessibility is not optional. WCAG 2.2 AA applies to internal tools and Power BI reports, as it does to public services.
3. Plain English and the GOV.UK style guide apply to every word in a report: titles, visual titles, labels, tooltips and empty states.
4. Follow the Government Analysis Function data visualisation guidance for charts, tables and colour (see `general/data-visualisation.mdc`).
5. GOV.UK Frontend is only used for the password page in `server.js` and the hub pages (`public/index.html`, `public/versions/`). Don't add GOV.UK components to the report pages. They would show users something Power BI can't produce.
6. Use invented data only. Never put real site names, permit numbers, carrier registrations or people's names into a prototype, ticket or screenshot.
